# Vibe Hub copy (Finder)

Code lives in `~/vibe`. Franky also wants a Files-visible copy at:

`~/Desktop/VIBE HUB copy`

Do **not** treat that folder as a second codebase. Do **not** write app code there.

After a session that changed any of: `brand/`, `public/html/`, `public/journal/`, `DOCS/`, `handoffs/`, `otto_mockups/`, or the Obsidian brand note — run:

```bash
bash ~/vibe/scripts/sync-vibe-hub.sh
```

Also run it at the end of a session if you created docs, a brand kit, a handoff, or HTML prototypes.

The Desktop `sync.command` does the same copy (vibe → hub). The old direction (hub HTML → `public/html`) is retired.
